I walk into the small room.
The official sits at the desk.
"Good morning," I say.
"Good morning," the official says.
"Do you have your passport?" he asks.
I show him my passport.
He checks the passport.
"Your name is Maya Flores?" he asks.
"Yes, that is correct," I answer.
He works at the computer.
He registers the flat as my address.
"Do you have a German telephone number?" the official asks.
"No, I do not have a German telephone number yet," I answer.
"That is no problem," he says.
He prints a document.
He stamps the paper.
"Here is your registration," he says.
"Thank you very much," I say and put the registration into my backpack.
